------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY EVIDENCE (web -> native, symbol)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[comp]  AnimatedNumber (@/components/data-display) -> count-up Animatable + the
        shared ChartFormat.number formatter, rendered at displaySmall in valueColor
        (the web styles the atom via className text-3xl font-bold {valueColor};
        the parameterless data-display atom cannot express valueColor, so the glyph
        is rendered directly to preserve that knob — documented in WidgetBigNumber.kt).
[comp]  Badge (@/components/ui) -> io.teslasync.android.components.ui.Badge.
[logic] badgeVariantMap {success,warning,error->danger,neutral}
                                 -> WidgetBigNumberBadgeVariant.toBadgeVariant.
[logic] value !== null ? (animated ? AnimatedNumber : tabular span) : nullDisplay
                                 -> WidgetBigNumberValue when-branches over
                                    WidgetBigNumberModel.project.
[logic] fmtNumber + tabular-nums -> ChartFormat.number + fontFeatureSettings "tnum".
[style] text-3xl font-bold        -> typography.displaySmall (30sp Bold); valueColor -> Color param.
[style] unit text-lg secondary    -> titleMedium / onSurfaceVariant.
[style] label text-[10px] uppercase muted -> labelSmall + uppercase(locale) + muted color.
[style] subtitle text-xs secondary -> bodySmall / onSurfaceVariant.
[style] null muted (text-muted)   -> onSurfaceVariant @ 0.7 alpha.
[state] present(animated) -> count-up glyph; present(static, animated=false) -> static glyph;
        null/non-finite -> muted nullDisplay glyph (web value===null branch);
        unit/label/subtitle/badge each render only when present (web `x && …`).
[a11y]  one merged contentDescription (value+unit, label, subtitle, badge) read once by
        TalkBack; testTag root; type tokens respect font scale; reduced motion honored.
[telem] view.opened slug=WidgetBigNumber -> WidgetBigNumberDiagnostics.recordViewOpened (P1/S11).
[i18n]  none — the primitive is anonymous; every visible string is a caller prop, exactly
        as the web source (which has no t() calls). No key invented (covenant: no silent drift).

States rationale: this is a PURE presentational primitive (no hooks, no fetch). Its real,
fully-reproduced states are the value branches above. The generic loading/error/stale/offline
states do not apply (there is no async feed); the owning widget wraps this primitive in its own
shell carrying those states (e.g. RangeBarWidget's WidgetShell). Fabricating them would model a
dependency the web spec does not have (covenant: no scope narrowing / no skip-and-assume).

Note on tests: the GATE runs :android:testReleaseUnitTest only — the pure projection (9) +
diagnostics (2) = 11 JVM tests cover the adapter, every value state, and the PII-safe telemetry.
The instrumented WidgetBigNumberUiTest (per-state render + a11y contentDescription) needs an
emulator the gate does not start. It compiles clean: a full :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin
reports 59 PRE-EXISTING errors across OTHER artifacts' androidTest files (missing assertExists/
assertDoesNotExist imports, @Composable misuse — e.g. FSMStateDiagram, NotionSidebar, TreeSelect,
BatteryCellsWidget) and ZERO attributable to WidgetBigNumberUiTest.kt. Those files are outside this
artifact's allowed files / out of scope (each surface has its own prompt) and the androidTest source
set is not part of this gate, so they are left untouched (no predecessor bypass, no out-of-scope edits).
The 3 @Preview render the full/empty/static states for visual verification.

